TROE shared data
================

/share contains immutable, architecture-independent data shipped with TROE.
Each producer owns a directory named /share/<producer> so examples, templates,
schemas, themes, and similar assets remain easy to find and cannot collide.

Executables belong in /bin, persistent or mounted data in /vol, and future
native shared libraries in /lib. The current recovery KEFS keeps bootstrap
files in /etc. The future package-managed namespace instead uses writable
desired configuration in /config and exposes the active generation's resolved,
non-secret configuration read-only in /sys/config; /etc is not a package ABI.
